title: Motions against the Natsir cabinet
subtitle: The cabinet's position is being tested..
new-page: true
tags: event
max-visits: 1
view-if: irian_motion_timer = 1
go-to: djody_motion if month = 12 and year = 1950; kusnan_motion if month != 12 or year != 1950;

@djody_motion

= The Crisis over West Irian

With the Hague Conference concluding in failure, tensions between the cabinet and the opposition have only flared up. 

In parliament, there was widespread agreement that the Netherlands-Indonesian Union, which had acquired little reality in the year it had been in existence, should be liquidated. And some kind of revision of the Round Table Conference agreements was called for by almost all groups of parliamentarians. There were, however, differences of emphasis between the viewpoints of government-supporting and opposition parties.

These differences eventually came to the fore as a motion has been placed before the House. The motion of five government-supporting parties was moved by Djody Gondokusumo of the <span style="color: #545454;">**PRN**</span>. It urged the government:

> *(1) to be prepared to conduct further negotiations with the Netherlands on the basis of the transfer of Indonesian sovereignty over West Irian;* <br>
> *(2) to give the Netherlands at most two months to answer the Indonesian demand as in (1) above; and* <br>
> *(3) to abrogate the Union Statute and review the results of the Round Table Conference and other agreements with the Netherlands with a view to abrogating all agreements which are damaging to Indonesia if there is no Dutch answer, or no satisfactory Dutch answer, within the time stipulated above.*

The cabinet expressed that there was little difference between its own standpoint and that incorporated in the Djody motion. It stated that it would negotiate with the Netherlands only on the basis of the transfer of sovereignty over Irian. And it said it would appoint a Special State Commission to examine the Round Table Conference agreements with a view to seeing how they could be brought into line with the new situation created by the failure of the Irian negotiations. Thereupon Djody withdrew his motion. 

- @kusnan: But wait, there's more..

@kusnan
on-arrival: psii_relation += 5;

Another slightly stronger motion put on the same time as Djody's was that of our Rahendra Kusnan, signed by <span style="color: #990000;">**PNI**</span> and <span style="color: #003319;">**PSII**</span> members. It urged the government:

> *(1) to continue to demand the immediate incorporation of West Irian into the territory of the Republic of Indonesia, on the basis of it having the same status as other areas of Indonesia;* <br>
> *(2) to abolish the Netherlands-Indonesian Union; and* <br>
> *(3) to review the other results of the Round Table Conference within three months with a view to obtaining their abrogation.* <br>

A vote was taken on the Kusnan motion. 

- @kusnan_nay: The voting commences..

